Feature: Epic 110 VRA Environmental Impact Assessment
  As an ESG Manager or Environmental Auditor
  I want carbon footprint accounting and water body protection strategies for VRA
  So that I can verify the environmental benefits of precision operations and comply with green standards

  @US-110-01 @ESG @Carbon
  Scenario: VRA-driven carbon footprint reduction accounting
    Given a series of variable-rate interventions
    When the ESG manager requests a "Carbon Impact Report"
    Then the system must quantify the reduction in emissions from fertilizer manufacturing savings
    And include the fuel savings from optimized machine paths compared to traditional grid spraying

  @US-110-02 @Compliance @Water
  Scenario: Automated water body buffer zone protection during VRA
    Given a GIS-defined water body or sensitive environmental zone
    When a VRA prescription is generated for a parcel nearby
    Then the system must automatically apply "Buffer Zone Rules" (e.g. zero application within 20m)
    And highlight these exclusion zones on the prescription map with a high-priority warning

  @US-110-03 @Soil @Health
  Scenario: Soil health aware VRA and degradation prevention
    Given a parcel with recorded soil health indices (e.g. pH, organic matter)
    When the VRA engine calculates the target dosage
    Then it must automatically adjust the prescription to avoid over-acidification or nutrient imbalance
    And provide long-term soil health management suggestions based on the VRA history
